<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Position</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre><a cmd='#'>stand</a>   stand up
<a cmd='#'>sit</a>     sit down
<a cmd='#'>rest</a>    lie down and rest
<a cmd='#'>sleep</a>   go to sleep
<a cmd='#'>wake</a>    wake up; wake &lt;someone&gt; wakes them
</pre>
<p>These commands change your position. To move around by yourself you must be 
standing.
</p><p>You heal, and get your mana and endurance back, faster when you aren't on your 
feet: half again as fast when you rest or sleep, a quarter faster when you sit. 
Resting heals as fast as sleeping, so there is no benefit to sleeping, and you 
can still see and talk while you rest. In a holy place, like the Temple of 
Udgaard, you heal twice as fast. In a fight you don't heal at all.
</p><p>But the further down you are, the more vulnerable you are to attacks. And 
someone who needs to be carried away (see <a cmd='#'>Help Drag</a>) must be asleep.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Regenerate</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Drag</a>
</pre>




</div>